Subject: [PATCH 2/2] boxpointer: Re-enable unredirect on destroy

Some popovers should show on top of unredirected fullscreen windows,
so we disable unredirection accordingly.

But it is flawed to purely rely on property notifications to undo the
inhibition, as ClutterActor stops emitting those on destroy. That means
that direct scanout is effectively disabled permantently if a boxpointer
is destroyed while visible.

Fix this by also re-enabling unredirect on destroy.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-shell/-/merge_requests/4470>
---
 js/ui/boxpointer.js | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/js/ui/boxpointer.js b/js/ui/boxpointer.js
index 7e5fff89d5..41c3a80175 100644
--- a/js/ui/boxpointer.js
+++ b/js/ui/boxpointer.js
@@ -55,6 +55,13 @@ export const BoxPointer = GObject.registerClass({
                 global.compositor.enable_unredirect();
         });
 
+        this.connect('destroy', () => {
+            // ClutterActor stops doing property notifications
+            // in destroy, so explicitly restore unredirect
+            if (this.mapped)
+                global.compositor.enable_unredirect();
+        });
+
         this._muteKeys = new Clutter.KeyController();
         this._muteKeys.connect('key-press', () => Clutter.EVENT_STOP);
         this.add_action_full(
